  "notes": "Whole-chain read support (>= 3 primary reads carrying the entire intron chain, same BAM the callers used) lifts UNKNOWN-support isoforms to NOVEL_PROBABLE. It separates caller-level false chains (FLAIR, IsoQuant: their false novels mostly lack full-chain reads) from alignment-level ones (Bambu, ESPRESSO, TALON: their false novels are carried by reads too), so the lift is a recall gain at little precision cost for the former and a precision cost for the latter. Non-independent evidence by construction: it never reaches NOVEL_CONFIRMED and never overrides a short-read verdict. SIRV-Set4 (second truth set, PBSIM3 reads): read level replicates, flair: genuine 8/12 vs false 13/178 with >= 3 full-chain reads; isoquant: genuine 5/6 vs false 0/4 with >= 3 full-chain reads. Engine level not evaluable there: SQANTI3 classifies most FLAIR SIRV models antisense/intergenic (genuine chains by category: {'antisense': 7, 'novel_not_in_catalog': 4, 'intergenic': 1}), which PanIsoGuard does not adjudicate, and the adjudicated NNC carry mapping/noncanonical signs from the simulated reads, so ON == OFF.",
